  "text": " Pigs Make Me Sneeze by Mo Willems. Pigs Make Me Sneeze. Gerald! What do you want to do today? I want... Yes? A what? A ball? A swim? A hat? A cow! Are you okay? I don't know. Achoo! I cannot stop. Achoo! Sneezing. Oh, no! What if... what if... what if pigs make me sneeze? Achoo! What if you try to sneeze more softly? Sorry. But if pigs do make me sneeze, then I cannot be near you! Then we cannot be friends. Then we must be apart forever. But, Gerald. No, do not speak. It is too late. Shoo. Goodbye. Gerald. Are you okay, Gerald? No, I'm not okay, Dr. Cat. Pigs make me sneeze! And Piggy is a pig. Piggy is also my best friend. Chew! Great, now cats make me sneeze too. I don't think pigs make you sneeze. I don't think cats make you sneeze. I think you have a cold. A cold? You are sick. I am sick! Oh, thank you, Dr. Cat. Piggy, piggy, great news! I have a cold! Good for you. This book is amazing. I love this book very much because Gerald would rather having a cold but not losing his friends. You understand that? Yeah! It's coming. It's amazing.",
